    five_star_ratings: 0,
    long_description:
      "Ludo Super King: The game of kings\nLudo Super King is a dice game that's challenging, exciting, easy to learn, but hard to master—and it's a whole lot of fun. The game is multiplayer, so you can challenge your friends or family members to see who can win. If you want something new and exciting to play with your friends or family members, this is an excellent choice! It's fun, it's challenging, and it's great for playing against friends and family.\nThis version of Ludo game is so much better than the original, you'll be surprised by how much fun it is. \nYou and your friends are going to love this one. Ludo Super King has been designed from the ground up for play with family and friends, so everyone can get in on the action. It's simple enough for kids to play by themselves, but challenging enough that even adults will find themselves having great games with their children.\n\nHistory\nLudo has its roots in the Indian game Pachisi, which is considered to be one of the earliest forms of the game. However, Ludo is considered to be a simplifies version of Pachisi, with more straightforward ruled and easier gameplay.\n \nMode\nLudo Super King is a multiplayer board game designed for 2 to 4 players and can be played by people of all ages. You can play ludo super king game with your friends or family members!\n\nLudo Board\nA Ludo board is square with a pattern on it in the shape of a cross, each arm being divided into three adjacent columns of eight squares. The middle squares form the home column for each colour and cannot be landed upon by other colours. The middle of the cross forms a large square which is the 'home' area and which is divided into 4 home triangles, one of each colour. At each corner, separate to the main circuit are coloured circles (or squares) where the pieces are placed to begin.\nEach player chooses one of the 4 colours (green, yellow, red or blue) and places the 4 pieces of that colour in the corresponding starting circle. A single die is thrown to determine movement\n\nHow to Play\nEach player starts with four tokens, placed on the start square, and the objective is to move all four tokens from the start to the finish square as quickly as possible. The game is played on a board with a square grid pattern that consists of squares of different colors, including start, finish, and safe squares\nThe game is played with a single die, and players take turns rolling the die to determine their next move. On their turn, a player rolls the die and moves one of their tokens the number of squares indicated by the roll. If a player rolls a 6, they get another turn, and they can choose to move any of their tokens or roll the die again\nThe game also includes special squares on the board that offer various advantages and disadvantages. For example, landing on a safe square protects a player's token from being sent back to the start by an opponent, while landing on a penalty square sends a player's token back to the start. Additionally, the game includes special cards that offer unique abilities, such as allowing a player to move an extra space or skip an opponent's turn.\n\nWinning\nThe winner is the first person to place all four pieces in the winning triangle\n\nOverall, Ludo Super King is a simple but strategic game that combines luck and strategy. With its easy-to-learn rules and exciting gameplay, Ludo Super King is a great game for families and friends to play together. Whether you're looking for a fun game to pass the time or a competitive game to play with friends, Ludo is a classic game that is sure to provide hours of fun.",
